    "lawCode": "Add §93, State L",
    "lawSection": "State Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1889\n\nSPONSOR: ASHBY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state law, in relation to designating the state of\nNew York a purple heart state\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo amend the state law, in relation to designating the state of New York\na Purple Heart state.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. State law is amended by adding section 92. This designates\nthe state of New York as a Purple Heart State\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will designate New York State as a Purple Heart state,\nenshrining into law our gratitude for the sacrifices made by wounded\nVeterans.  New York State is already the proud home of the National\nPurple Heart Hall of Honor; designating New York State as a Purple Heart\nstate would solidify our commitment to wounded veterans of our state.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-24: S.4459- passed in Senate; died in Assembly\n\n2021-22: S.2279 - passed in Senate; died in Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of January next succeeding the\ndate upon which it shall become law.\n",
